        "math_academy_id": "q-86179",
        "problem": "Find ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$  for $f(x)=4\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(2x).$",
        "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of arcsine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(2x)) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(2x)) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(2x)^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "actual_result": "Correct",
